% Probe: can a PDF named destination be registered from an `inline-graphics`
% callback?
%
% Both engines now render this, and the anchor lands in both PDFs:
%
%   layout-tests/tools/probe.py layout-tests/probes/inline_graphics_dest.saty
%
%   SATySFi 0.0.11   /nameddest0 [<page 1> /XYZ 124.328    733.17776378 null]
%   this port        /nameddest0 [<page 1> /XYZ 124.975624 733.1769     0]
%
% The y agrees to 0.001pt; the 0.65pt in x is this document's ordinary
% text-advance delta for the word before the anchor, not an anchor error.
%
% It USED to be the port's loudest corpus blocker:
%
%   Error: register-destination can only be called during page breaking
%          (from a page-break hook or a decoration)
%
% Upstream and this port agree on the GATE --- `annotation.ml:15` raises
% `State.NotDuringPageBreak` outside the window too, so relaxing it would have
% been the unfaithful fix. They disagreed on WHEN the callback runs.
% `primitives.rs`'s `prim_inline_graphics` documents the deviation as its
% "eager-callback shortcut": a lang closure cannot live inside a
% `PureHorzBox::Graphics`, so the callback is applied once at construction
% time at `(0pt, 0pt)` (and a second time at a probe point, to detect a
% page-absolute callback) and the writer's per-box `cm` supplies the placed
% position later. That is exact for a shift-covariant graphics generator and
% was fatal for a SIDE-EFFECTING one: at construction time no page exists, so
% `interp.current_page` is `None` and the gate fired.
%
% The fix RE-TIMES the call rather than relaxing the gate. The eager
% application records it (`Interp::pending_dests`), the box carries it as a
% `GraphicsElem::Destination` marker, and `fire_hooks` --- which already
% recurses into a graphics box's elements --- replays it against the box's real
% page and placed point. Riding `elems` rather than a field of its own is what
% makes the ANCHOR-ONLY shape below work: its ink is `[]` at both call points,
% so on ink alone the box would be classified page-absolute and the anchor
% would never move to where the box landed.
%
% Pinned by `crates/rustyfi-lang/tests/inline_graphics_dest.rs`.
%
% Measured on azmath (satysfi-azmath 0.0.3), whose `equation.satyh`
% `ib-annotation` is exactly the shape below --- it anchors every `\label`ed
% equation, and this gap was the whole reason the port could not build its
% manual. It now builds unstubbed, with all 16 of upstream's named
% destinations present (14 pages, 571 lines against upstream's 15/583;
% char_match 0.9569).
@require: stdjabook

let-inline ctx \anchor key =
  inline-graphics 0pt 0pt 0pt (fun (x, y) -> (
    let () = register-destination key (x, y) in []
  ))
in

document (|
  title = {inline-graphics destination probe};
  author = {};
  show-title = false;
  show-toc = false;
|) '<
  +p{before \anchor(`probe-dest`); after}
>
